' F14 -- Trust boundaries and RLS policy patterns.
' Chapter 5 (Implementation). Concept diagram.
' Claim supported: authorisation is enforced in the database, not the API. Four
' distinct policy patterns cover 47 tables; effective visibility is the UNION
' of applicable policies, which is the structural hazard.
@startuml f14-trust-boundaries
!include _style.iuml

title Trust boundaries — where authorisation is actually enforced

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

rectangle "**UNTRUSTED**" as UT #DCDCDC {
  rectangle "Browser\n//holds the anon key,\nbaked into the bundle//" as BR
  rectangle "Uploaded PDF text\n//professor OR student//" as PDF #DCDCDC
}

rectangle "**Identity boundary**" as ID #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "Supabase Auth\nJWT issuer" as JWT
  rectangle "anon\n//no claims//" as ANON
  rectangle "authenticated\n//auth.uid() present//" as AUTH
  rectangle "service_role\n//bypasses RLS entirely//" as SR #BFBFBF
}

rectangle "**Postgres RLS — the real enforcement point**\n47 tables, 100% coverage, 198 policies" as RLS #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "**P1 Owner-scoped**\nuser_id = auth.uid()\n//xp_events, review_schedule,\nexam_attempts, notifications//" as P1
  rectangle "**P2 Role-gated ownership**\nowner = uid AND has_role(professor)\n//courses, lectures//" as P2
  rectangle "**P3 Enrollment-derived**\nEXISTS join via course_enrollments\nor assignment_lectures\n//slides, quiz_questions, review_cards//" as P3
  rectangle "**P4 Backend-only**\nno anon/authenticated policy at all\n//parse_runs, slide_embeddings, caches//" as P4 #DCDCDC
}

rectangle "FastAPI\n//holds the service_role key//" as API #F2F2F2

BR --> JWT
JWT --> ANON
JWT --> AUTH
ANON -[#1A1A1A,dashed]-> RLS : "**zero** table policies\ngrant TO anon"
AUTH --> P1
AUTH --> P2
AUTH --> P3
BR --> API
API --> SR
SR --> P4
PDF -[#1A1A1A,dashed]-> P3 : "content flows into\nanother user's\ntutor context"

note bottom of RLS
  **The structural hazard.** Postgres OR-combines permissive
  SELECT policies, so effective visibility is the UNION of every
  applicable policy — not the intersection. Called out explicitly
  in migration 20260719020000:25-29.

  **And it is untested end to end:** no test composes a real
  endpoint against real RLS (MILESTONE_2026_08.md:205-210), so the
  union behaviour that caused the original cross-tenant leak
  remains unguarded at the integration level.
end note

note right of P4
  service_role bypasses RLS, so
  every P4 table is protected only
  by the API's own checks. This is
  why lecture ownership is verified
  in chat_service before retrieval
  (see F12) — the database will not
  do it for this path.
end note

legend bottom
  Authorisation lives in the database. The API layer adds ownership checks on top for
  service_role paths, but is not the boundary. See F15 for how these policies were
  hardened across five migrations, and F4 for why uploaded content is untrusted.
endlegend

@enduml
